# Rules migrated → .cursor/rules/*.mdc

Cursor still loads this file on every turn, so it is intentionally kept thin.
The real rules are now scoped `.mdc` files under `.cursor/rules/`:

- `000-core.mdc`       — always-on protocol: knowledge-stack-first, think-before-coding,
                         goal-driven loops, surgical changes, report format
- `knowledge-stack.mdc`— full query-priority stack (ccc / graphify / wiki / decisions / interfaces / lessons)
- `ccc-search.mdc`     — ccc/cocoindex daemon operational guide (agent-requested)
- `embedded-c.mdc`     — STM32F4/FreeRTOS conventions + gotchas (auto-attaches on API/TASK/BSP/USER)

Custom commands: `.cursor/commands/` — type `/` in the Agent (session-start, session-end, diagnose, review).
Custom subagents: `.cursor/agents/` — `uav-conductor` (full pipeline orchestrator, Claude Opus 5
High), `uav-planner` (Claude Opus 5 High), `uav-implementer` (Cursor Grok 4.5 High Fast), and
`uav-reviewer` (GPT-5.6 Sol High, readonly). See `.cursor/agents/AGENTS.md` for the full index.
Hooks: `.cursor/hooks.json` + `.cursor/hooks/knowledge-gate.js` (nudges toward ccc before raw grep).
